  :body "# In-Browser AI IDE & Vibe Coder Architecture Specification

> **Subsystem**: `asl/web` • `harness` • `vdom` • `web-api-search`  
> **Target Route**: `/in-ide` (Hidden route, omitted from public sitemaps and navigation)  
> **Engine Substrate**: [InBrowserAddie.asl](file:///Users/purplelephant/projects/asex/asl/web/asl-src/components/InBrowserAddie.asl) (WebGPU SLM) + [model_calibration.asl](file:///Users/purplelephant/projects/asex/harness/src/model_calibration.asl)  
> **Configuration Source**: [in_browser_ide_config.asn](file:///Users/purplelephant/projects/asex/harness/calibration/in_browser_ide_config.asn)  
> **Status**: Verified Master Architecture Blueprint & Execution Plan (Phases 429–432)

---

## 1. Executive Concept & The \"Vibe Coder\" Paradigm

Traditional in-browser IDEs (e.g. StackBlitz, CodeSandbox, GitHub Codespaces) emulate desktop editors like VS Code by packing file trees, tab bars, terminal splitters, and dense code editors into the viewport. This legacy desktop-centric layout imposes heavy cognitive friction on conversational AI-assisted development.

The **In-Browser AI IDE (`/in-ide`)** fundamentally inverts this model through the **\"Vibe Coder\" Paradigm**:
1. **Hidden Code Editor by Default**: The developer drives software creation and iteration primarily through high-level conversational directives with the **Addie AI Agent** and structured action presets. The raw code editor is hidden behind an unobtrusive slide-out drawer (`[< > Code / VFS]`) or `Alt+C` toggle.
2. **Visual Feedback Foremost**: The central workspace is dominated by a live, zero-latency interactive viewport (HTML5 Canvas game, responsive iframe website, or native SVG diagram) that hot-reloads in-place upon each agent mutation.
3. **Receipt-Driven Visibility**: Rather than forcing the developer to parse thousands of lines of code, the agent outputs compact **1-line cryptographic execution receipts** and animated diff chips (`+18 -4 lines in /vfs/src/physics.asl`). Clicking any receipt smoothly slides open the editor directly to the affected AST hunk.
4. **Online-Only Browser Sovereignty**: The entire environment executes 100% inside the browser client without requiring external servers, Docker containers, or Node.js runtime daemons, while seamlessly binding to GitHub for repository sync.

