## 3. Universal OpenAI-Compatible Model Provider Configuration

In addition to local WebGPU execution, the In-IDE features a **Configurable Model Provider Hub** allowing developers to connect to any external OpenAI-compatible API endpoint:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        MODEL PROVIDER CONFIGURATION MODAL ()                               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Active Provider: [ OpenRouter ▾ ]  (Presets: Ollama, LM Studio, Groq, DeepSeek, OpenAI)
  
  Base URL:        [ https://openrouter.ai/api/v1                                           ]
  API Key:         [ sk-or-v1-•••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••••• ]
  Model Name:      [ qwen/qwen-2.5-coder-32b-instruct                                       ]
  
  Sampling Parameters:
  Temperature:     [ 0.2  ]   Max Tokens: [ 4096 ]   Top-P: [ 0.95 ]
  
  Connection Test: [  Ping Provider ]  -> Result:  Connected (142ms latency, Stream: OK)
  
  [ Cancel ]                                                           [ Save & Activate ]
```

### Key Provider Capabilities:
1. **Universal Endpoint Compatibility**:
   - **Local Daemons**: Ollama (`http://localhost:11434/v1`), LM Studio (`http://localhost:1234/v1`), Local Host Daemon (`http://localhost:4040/v1` via `asl daemon`).
   - **Cloud Providers**: OpenRouter, Groq, DeepSeek, Together AI, OpenAI, Google AI Studio Gemini API.
2. **Client-Side Credential Sovereignty**:
   - API keys are stored **strictly in client-side `localStorage` / encrypted session storage**.
   - Requests are dispatched directly from the browser using standard CORS `fetch()`. Zero credentials ever pass through an intermediary backend.
3. **Live Latency & Healthcheck Ping (`[Ping Provider]`)**:
   - Dispatches a lightweight 1-token test prompt (`\"Hi\"`) to verify latency, authentication, and Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming compatibility before committing.

