## 4. In-Browser Virtual File System (VFS) & File Management

The IDE includes a fully autonomous **In-Memory Virtual File System** operating under `/vfs/workspace/`:

```
/vfs/workspace/
├── package.asn              # ASL project manifest & dependencies
├── README.md                # Generated documentation & run instructions
├── src/
│   ├── main.asl             # Application entrypoint & state machine
│   ├── game_engine.asl      # Core 2D canvas physics & game loop
│   └── components/
│       ├── Header.asl       # VDOM navigation header
│       └── Mascot.asl       # Procedural SVG mascot sprite
└── assets/
    └── style.css            # Scoped Tailwind / custom styling
```

### VFS Operational Invariants:
1. **Multi-Buffer Content Addressing**: Every file buffer maintains a content-addressable SHA-256 hash (`#cas`), tracking clean vs. dirty status.
2. **Atomic In-Memory Patches**: When the agent mutates a file, changes are applied to the in-memory buffer with transaction rollback protection. If the code throws an uncaught syntax or runtime exception in the viewport, the buffer automatically rolls back to the last known good state.
3. **Drawer Integration**: The file tree is concealed by default. When toggled (`Alt+C`), a sleek glassmorphic sidebar slides in from the left, offering file creation, renaming, deletion, and real-time AST outline inspection.

