## 5. Google AI Studio-Style Export & In-Browser GitHub Integration

The In-IDE provides friction-free export and bidirectional version control directly from the browser tab without requiring git CLI binaries or server bridges:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    VFS[\"In-Memory VFS (/vfs/workspace/)\"] --> ExportHub[\"Export & Sync Engine\"]

    ExportHub -->|Instant Download| ZipExport[\"ZIP Archive (.zip via fflate Wasm)\"]
    ExportHub -->|Single File| FileExport[\"Raw Code (.asl, .asn, .svg, .js)\"]
    ExportHub -->|Portable Config| AsnExport[\"ASL Workspace Snapshot (.asn)\"]

    ExportHub -->|Direct GitHub REST API| GitHubSync[\"GitHub Integration (PAT Auth)\"]
    GitHubSync -->|Git Trees API| PullRepo[\"Pull / Clone Repo into VFS\"]
    GitHubSync -->|Git Commits API| PushCommit[\"Commit & Push to Branch\"]
    GitHubSync -->|Pulls API| CreatePR[\"Open Pull Request\"]
```

### 5.1. Client-Side Archive & Configuration Export
1. **Zero-Server ZIP Generation**:
   - Utilizes pure WebAssembly / JavaScript compression (`fflate`) running in a WebWorker.
   - Bundles all `/vfs/workspace/` files into a clean `project.zip` download in under 50ms.
2. **Single-File Raw Export**:
   - Instant 1-click download of individual `.asl`, `.asn`, `.html`, or `.svg` files with appropriate MIME types.
3. **Portable ASL Configuration Export (`.asn`)**:
   - Exports the complete workspace state—including active model profile, system prompts, VFS manifest, and action history—as a standardized AgentScript configuration file (`workspace_snapshot.asn`), allowing instant reconstitution in another browser.

### 5.2. Direct In-Browser GitHub Integration
- **Authentication**: User provides a fine-grained GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT) with `repo` scope (persisted in browser storage).
- **Clone / Pull**:
  - Queries `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/trees/{branch}?recursive=1` and fetches file blobs directly into `/vfs/workspace/`.
- **Commit & Push**:
  - Constructs blobs (`POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/blobs`), builds a tree (`POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/trees`), creates a commit (`POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/commits`), and updates the branch reference (`PATCH /repos/{owner}/{repo}/git/refs/heads/{branch}`).
  - **100% Client-Side**: No Node.js server or Docker container required.
- **1-Click Pull Request**:
  - Automatically creates a new branch (`addie-patch-{timestamp}`), commits changes, and opens a Pull Request (`POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls`).

